<h2>Customer Experience Should be a Top Priority</h2>
<p style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px;">A study recently undertaken by <a href="https://blog.smart-tribune.com/en/customer-expectations" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Zendesk</a> found that 21% of 18 to 24 year olds claim to have higher expectations in terms of customer service interactions, compared to only 11% of consumers over the age of 55. As the digital-first generations continue to grow in numbers, higher expectations will naturally increase.</p>
<p style="color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 16px;">In a world where competition is so fierce within retail, and where consumers will happily choose an alternative retailer if they suffer a poor experience, high quality customer service should be a prime priority for businesses. </p>
